---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { mcpUrl, clients, prompts } from '../data/mcp';
import '../styles/global.css'

const appUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_APP_URL ?? 'http://localhost:8081';

const toolGroups = [
	{
		title: 'Plan and build',
		tools: ['plan_notebook', 'search_tools', 'create_notebook', 'add_cell', 'update_cell', 'delete_cell'],
		description: 'Plan an analysis, find ready-made tools, and write SQL, Python, Markdown, chart and input cells.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Run',
		tools: ['run_notebook', 'get_run_results', 'get_environment_status', 'restart_environment'],
		description: 'Run a notebook or single cells and read back tables, chart summaries and errors.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Manage notebooks',
		tools: ['search_notebooks', 'get_notebook', 'edit_notebook', 'fork_notebook', 'publish_notebook', 'unpublish_notebook', 'schedule_notebook', 'unschedule_notebook', 'delete_notebook'],
		description: 'Find, rename, fork, publish, schedule and delete notebooks.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Data and files',
		tools: ['list_data_sources', 'get_data_source_schema', 'upload_file', 'list_files', 'read_file', 'delete_file', 'set_env_vars', 'delete_env_var'],
		description: 'See which data sources are available, upload files, and store API keys as environment variables.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Workspaces and comments',
		tools: ['list_workspaces', 'create_workspace', 'list_projects', 'list_comments', 'add_comment', 'delete_comment', 'save_reply'],
		description: 'Choose a workspace, leave comments, and save the agent\'s closing message to the notebook\'s chat.',
	},
];

const troubleshooting = [
	{
		q: 'SSE error: Non-200 status code (405)',
		a: 'The client is set to the SSE transport. Remove the server and add it again as HTTP (streamable HTTP).',
	},
	{
		q: 'It says the server needs authentication',
		a: 'Sign in from the client (in Claude Code: /mcp, pick sandworm, authenticate). A browser window opens on Sandworm to approve access.',
	},
	{
		q: 'A SQL cell failed',
		a: 'Ask the agent to rebuild the notebook "using open data". It will fetch from public APIs in Python instead.',
	},
];

const h2 = 'text-2xl font-medium mt-10 mb-4 text-white';
const pre = 'rounded-xl bg-hero-base border border-white/10 p-4 text-sm text-[#C5CED9] overflow-x-auto font-mono';
const inline = 'text-[#C7C2FF] font-mono text-sm';
---

<Layout
	title="MCP docs | Sandworm"
	description="Connect Claude, Cursor or any MCP client to Sandworm and let your agent build, run and publish onchain analysis notebooks."
	path="/mcp"
>
	<Header solid />
	<main class="bg-black text-[#7D8791] min-h-screen p-8 font-body pt-28 lg:pt-36 pb-20">
		<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-4">
			<h1 class="lg:text-4xl text-3xl font-bold mb-4 text-[#C7C2FF] font-mono uppercase">
				Sandworm MCP
			</h1>
			<p class="text-[#C5CED9]">
				Connect your AI agent to Sandworm. It can plan an analysis, write and run SQL and Python,
				build charts and publish the notebook, all from the chat. You get a notebook you can open,
				edit and re-run.
			</p>
			<p class="text-sm">
				These docs are an early draft and will change.
			</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>1. Server address</h2>
			<pre class={pre}><code>{mcpUrl}</code></pre>
			<p>
				Transport: HTTP (streamable HTTP). Sign-in: OAuth with your Sandworm account, so there is no
				API key to copy. You need a Sandworm account first:
				<a href={`${appUrl}/workspace`} class="text-[#C7C2FF] underline hover:text-white">create one here</a>.
			</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>2. Connect your client</h2>
			<div class="space-y-6">
				{clients.map(client => (
					<div>
						<h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-white mb-1">{client.name}</h3>
						<p class="mb-2">{client.note}</p>
						<pre class={pre}><code>{client.code}</code></pre>
					</div>
				))}
			</div>
			<p>
				The first time you connect, a Sandworm page opens in your browser asking you to approve access.
				The agent then works in your default workspace unless you name another.
			</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>3. Try it</h2>
			<p>Ask in plain language. Some prompts to start with:</p>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-[#C5CED9]">
				{prompts.map(prompt => <li>{prompt}</li>)}
			</ul>

			<h2 class={h2}>4. Choosing the data</h2>
			<p>A notebook can be built from two kinds of data. Say which you want in your prompt:</p>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
				<li>
					<strong class="text-white">Sandworm data and tools</strong> ("using our tools", "using Dune"):
					chain data queried with SQL, plus ready-made power tools.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="text-white">Open data</strong> ("using open data", "public APIs"):
					public sources such as DefiLlama, CoinGecko and growthepie, fetched in Python cells.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				If you say nothing, Sandworm data is used, and open data is the fallback when chain SQL is not available.
			</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>5. What the agent can do</h2>
			<div class="space-y-5">
				{toolGroups.map(group => (
					<div>
						<h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-white mb-1">{group.title}</h3>
						<p class="mb-2">{group.description}</p>
						<p class="leading-7">
							{group.tools.map((tool, i) => (
								<Fragment><code class={inline}>{tool}</code>{i < group.tools.length - 1 ? ', ' : ''}</Fragment>
							))}
						</p>
					</div>
				))}
			</div>

			<h2 class={h2}>6. Session history</h2>
			<p>
				Every MCP session is saved to the notebook's chat in Sandworm: your request, the plan, each cell
				the agent created or ran, and its closing message. Open the notebook and its chat panel to see
				what the agent did. Values that look like secrets are redacted.
			</p>

			<h2 class={h2}>7. Troubleshooting</h2>
			<dl class="space-y-4">
				{troubleshooting.map(item => (
					<div>
						<dt class="text-white font-medium">{item.q}</dt>
						<dd class="mt-1">{item.a}</dd>
					</div>
				))}
			</dl>

			<p class="pt-6">
				Questions or something broken? Ask in our
				<a href="https://discord.gg/pftQtpcjK2" class="text-[#C7C2FF] underline hover:text-white" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Discord</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>
